<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady in dull trade.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady in dull trade.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady in dull trade on Friday on limited arrivals with some markets being closed, traders said.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent fell by 200 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined was down by 100 rupees on increased selling pressure against poor demand, they said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices gained at record levels on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $285-286 per tonne for current season and was $270 for November-December 1996 shipment.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $120-121 in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,050-4,100 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,000-4,050 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
